      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <cstddef>\n\nstatic long long maximum_horizontal_sum(const std::vector<long long>& columns,\n                                        int n, int s) {\n    long long sum = 0;\n    for (int j = 0; j < s; ++j)\n        sum += columns[j];\n\n    long long maximum = sum;\n    for (int j = s; j < n; ++j) {\n        sum += columns[j] - columns[j - s];\n        if (sum > maximum)\n            maximum = sum;\n    }\n    return maximum;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n    std::vector<int> matrix(static_cast<std::size_t>(n) * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        int* row = &matrix[static_cast<std::size_t>(i) * n];\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n            scanf(\"%d\", row + j);\n    }\n\n    assert(s < n);\n    assert(n < 8000);\n    assert(s > 0);\n    assert(n > 0);\n\n    std::vector<long long> columnSums(n, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i < s; ++i) {\n        const int* row = &matrix[static_cast<std::size_t>(i) * n];\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n            columnSums[j] += row[j];\n    }\n\n    long long mxSum = maximum_horizontal_sum(columnSums, n, s);\n    for (int top = 1; top <= n - s; ++top) {\n        const int* outgoing = &matrix[static_cast<std::size_t>(top - 1) * n];\n        const int* incoming = &matrix[static_cast<std::size_t>(top + s - 1) * n];\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n            columnSums[j] += static_cast<long long>(incoming[j]) - outgoing[j];\n\n        const long long rowMaximum = maximum_horizontal_sum(columnSums, n, s);\n        if (rowMaximum > mxSum)\n            mxSum = rowMaximum;\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Contiguous row scans and reusable column totals should improve locality and reduce computation from O(S*N^2) to O(N^2), without changing input parsing.",
